<title>DENMARK: BG Bank buys Sydbank Luxembourg.</title>
<headline>BG Bank buys Sydbank Luxembourg.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's third biggest BG Bank said on Tuesday it purchased Sydbank Luxembourg S.A., the Luxembourg branch of Denmark's fifth biggest bank, with effect from January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>No purchase price was divulged but BG Bank said the merger meant it would buy the entire share capital in Sydbank Luxembourg, paying in addition 37 million crowns for goodwill.</p>
<p>BG Bank said the takeover was part of its strategy to strengthen its position in Luxembourg.</p>
<p>Sydbank Luxembourg had a pre-tax result of 8.9 million crowns for 1996's first six months, with own capital of 138.3 million crowns at the beginning of 1996, it said.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
